Buying the dip replaces market timing attempts when broad sell-offs hit without fundamental

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:57.540
deterioration in holdings. Today's geopolitical headlines and index declines create exactly

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:03.680
that setup. Investors who add to quality names on weakness have historically captured rebounds

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.660
once the shock passes. Implementation starts with a pre-built watch list of holdings already

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:19.200
in your TFSSA or RRSP. Then use a simple rule. Add only when price drops 5-8% from your last entry

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:25.820
and volume exceeds the 20-day average. The approach worked best in 2018 and 2022,

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.100
volatility spikes when investors maintain dry powder rather than selling into fear.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.800
Risks include catching a falling knife if the catalyst proves structural,

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:40.620
so position size remains caped at 5% of the account per addition.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:45.360
Always confirm the dip aligns with your original thesis before executing.

