00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:57.900
Imagine you just received a $10,000 windfall and want to put it to work in your TFSA before the

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:04.640
contribution room resets. The first step is confirming your emergency fund covers three to six months

00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:11.640
of expenses in a high interest savings account. Only then move to investing. Most Canadians start with

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:19.760
the TFSA over an RRSP because of tax-free growth and flexible withdrawals. Then decide between a

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:29.120
single all equity ETF like VEQT for simplicity or a three ETF mix of Canadian, US and international

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:36.100
equity for modest diversification. Open the account at wealth simple or quest trade. Link your bank

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:41.620
and place the first purchase as a limit order during market hours rather than a market order to

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:49.180
avoid slippage. Set up automatic $200 by weekly contributions the same day so the psychological barrier

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:55.960
of pressing buy is crossed once. Historical data shows broad equity markets have delivered roughly

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:02.500
seven to eight percent annualized returns over long periods. Yet single years can range from plus

00:07:02.500 --> 00:07:11.060
30% to minus 20%. So expect volatility rather than smooth gains. Before we wrap keep an eye on energy

